+# Incidents brief
+
+## 11 August 2026: ingest stall and full disk
+
+**Impact:** Data intake stopped for about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+
+**Root cause:** A malformed batch jammed intake in endless retries; their logs filled the database disk, halting writes.
+
+**Fix:** Restarted intake with the bad batch set aside; cleaned up the database and logs.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80%: Sunil. Done (30 Sep meeting).
+- Fix so a bad batch cannot jam intake: Jonas. Open, in review.
+- Paging escalation rules: Elif. Done (2 Sep meeting; tightened 16 Sep).
+
+## 21 September 2026: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** Public API down for 47 minutes on a Monday morning; nearly all clients failed to connect.
+
+**Root cause:** The certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently for weeks because it held an outdated credential.
+
+**Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API. The renewal job is repaired and alerts on failure.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry: Priya. Done (30 Sep meeting).
+- Alert on days left: Priya. Open.
+- Certificate check in weekly checklist: Tomasz. Open.
+- Responders record steps as they work: Mara. Done (handover notes, 30 Sep meeting).
